\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535145 true] [17592186333712 1113 #uuid "bab81a0a-80d6-5b73-892c-7e2e8306cdc8" 13194139535145 true] [17592186333712 1145 "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nComparing $A$ with the rotation matrix, we have \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta >0$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta <0$ we must have that $\\theta $ lies in $4$th quadrant. \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nThe principal value $\\theta $ is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ radians *clockwise* about the origin." 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333714 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333715 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333716 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333717 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333718 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1041 "selection" 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333717 13194139535145 true] [17592186333713 1110 #uuid "3e42b180-bf50-5a98-b370-2597672c5945" 13194139535145 true] [17592186333714 1034 "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin." 13194139535145 true] [17592186333714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535145 true] [17592186333714 1111 #uuid "6aa8e6d2-38ca-59a3-a169-2cb831e